## Third-party notice — read this before redistributing

This repository is **not an original work**. It is a port/adaptation of someone
else's project, and the split is:

| Part | Who made it | Licence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `index.js`, `client.js`, `package.json`, `cordis.patch.yml`, `tools/`, `test/`, this documentation | written for this repository by an **AI coding assistant** | MIT (above) |
| Everything under `assets/` — the sprite, the four expression sheets, `rice.png`, `iron_bowl.webp`, `hit.mp3`, `feed.mp3` | the **original author, VKmich16** | © VKmich16, not MIT |
| Everything under `reference/` — the original desktop widget's scripts and manuals | the **original author, VKmich16** | © VKmich16, not MIT |

`assets/flash.png` is the one asset generated here: it is a flat red silhouette
derived from the original sprite by `tools/make_flash.ps1`.

The original work:

- Author: **VKmich16**
- GitHub: <https://github.com/VKmich16/VK-1>
- Bilibili: **VKmich16**
  (<https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1cYa56fEyR/>,
  <https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1ZjHi6XEAp/>)
- What it is: the Windows desktop widget "DSH 余额宠物" (PowerShell + WinForms +
  GDI+), whose behaviour this plugin reproduces inside DeepSeek Harness.

So: **the code here is the AI port; the idea and the artwork are VKmich16's.**
Keep both credits when you pass this on.

If you do not have the right to redistribute the assets or the original scripts,
delete `assets/` and `reference/` before publishing and supply your own artwork —
the plugin code itself does not depend on their content, only on the file names
and the size relationships documented in `client.js`.


